.TH CUSTOM-TOOLBOX 1 "2026-07-20" "MX Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
custom-toolbox \- create and launch custom application toolboxes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B custom-toolbox
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file.list ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B custom-toolbox
creates a graphical launcher from a text file with the
.B .list
extension. Files are normally stored in
.IR /etc/custom-toolbox ,
but a file in another location may be opened by giving its path on the command line.
The application supports a key-value format and an INI format. Only entries with a matching desktop file are shown.
.PP
The key-value format uses fields such as
.B Name
,
.B Comment
,
.B Category
and application entries. Application entries may use the
.B root
,
.B user
,
.B terminal
and
.B alias="..."
flags. The INI format uses
.B [General]
,
.B [Categories]
, and category sections with comma-separated
.B items
entries; flags are separated by colons.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -r , " " --remove-checkbox
Do not show the startup checkbox asking whether the dialog should be shown again.
.TP
.BR -h , " " --help
Show help for the command.
.TP
.BR -v , " " --version
Show the application version.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I file.list
The full path of a custom toolbox file to load. If omitted, the application opens a file chooser.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/custom-toolbox
Default directory for toolbox files and examples.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR desktop-file-edit (1)
.SH AUTHOR
MX Linux contributors.
